# Open this file in PhpStorm HTTP Client and run requests using the gutter arrows.
# Edit variables here or edit each JSON body directly before sending a request.
# Use a NEW payrollLineId for each full run. Keep the same ID for steps 1-10.
# Running an adjustment twice applies it twice; there is no automatic reset.
# Amounts must remain quoted JSON strings. Expected amounts below use the defaults.

@baseUrl = http://localhost/api/v1
@payrollLineId = manual-payroll-002
@initialAmount = 1000.00
@recalculatedAmount = 1050.00
@adjustmentAmount = -45.55
@adjustmentComment = Unpaid leave

### 1. Create a payroll line — expected current amount 1000.00
POST {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": "{{payrollLineId}}",
  "amount": "{{initialAmount}}"
}

### 2. Recalculate before manual override — expected 1050.00
POST {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}/recalculations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "amount": "{{recalculatedAmount}}"
}

### 3. Apply an adjustment — edit the amount and comment above or directly here; expected 1004.45
POST {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "amount": "{{adjustmentAmount}}",
  "comment": "{{adjustmentComment}}"
}

### 4. Attempt recalculation after manual override — ignored; expected 1004.45
POST {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}/recalculations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "amount": "1200.00"
}

### 5. Apply a bonus — expected 1104.55
POST {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "amount": "100.10",
  "comment": "Bonus"
}

### 6. Apply correction A — expected 1104.45
POST {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "amount": "-0.10",
  "comment": "Correction A"
}

### 7. Apply correction B — expected 1104.25
POST {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "amount": "-0.20",
  "comment": "Correction B"
}

### 8. Compensate correction B — expected 1104.45
POST {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "amount": "0.20",
  "comment": "Reverse correction B"
}

### 9. Read the current amount — safe to repeat
GET {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}
Accept: application/json

### 10. Read the full audit — expected baseline 1050.00 and five adjustments; safe to repeat
GET {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines/{{payrollLineId}}/adjustments
Accept: application/json

### 11. List current states — one query without reading event history
GET {{baseUrl}}/payroll-lines?per_page=100&page=1
Accept: application/json
